  "verbalization": "Isoliquiritigenin appears to have a potential relationship with Dynamin-1 through a series of target-mediated pathways. The evidence suggests that Isoliquiritigenin acts as a target of multiple enzymes, including Electron transfer flavoprotein-ubiquinone oxidoreductase, UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B10, and UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B15, which in turn target Dynamin-1. These findings indicate a possible indirect mechanism by which Isoliquiritigenin may influence Dynamin-1, possibly through the modulation of enzyme activity that ultimately affects Dynamin-1 function. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The presence of multiple distinct targets that ultimately converge on Dynamin-1 implies a complex regulatory network, which may involve both direct and indirect pathways. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that Isoliquiritigenin could exert a biological effect on Dynamin-1, though further experimental validation is required to confirm the mechanism and its relevance in a clinical context.",
